340783"} {"question" "q-114030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/25)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/25}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$ \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get  \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "97c12285f778ab2b8c173ba1373eccc72c7b5e33b5d6af5d775f6efd34340783"} {"question" "q-114030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31e77975055356dfb2474618c3afed650e3c461761c728a631bc7a95a0837710"} {"question" "q-114030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.